      "text": "The median is the middle number of a sorted, ascending or descending, list of numbers. If there is an even number of observations, then the median is the average of the two middle numbers. In this set, there are 5 numbers, which is an odd number, so the median will be the third number when the set is sorted.\n\nTo find the median, we need to arrange the numbers in ascending order:\n\\[n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15\\]\n\nSince the median is 9, we can set up the equation for the middle number:\n\\[n + \\frac{9 - 5}{2} = 9\\]\n\\[n + 2 = 9\\]\n\\[n = 7\\]\n\nNow that we know \\(n = 7\\), we can substitute it back into the set:\n\\[\\{7, 12, 13, 16, 22\\}\\]\n\nThe median is the middle number, which is 13. The mean of the set is found by adding all the numbers and dividing by the number of elements:\n\\[\\text{Mean} = \\frac{7 + 12 + 13 + 16 + 22}{5} = \\frac{70}{5} = 14\\]\n\nTherefore, the mean of the set is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
