      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The median of a set is the middle value when the numbers are arranged in ascending order. Given that the median of the set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ is 9, we need to determine the value of $n$.\n\nSince the median is the middle value when the numbers are arranged in ascending order, and the set consists of 5 numbers, the median will be the third number in the ordered list. Therefore, we need the third number in the set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ to be 9.\n\nThis means:\n\\[ n + 6 = 9 \\]\n\nSolving for $n$:\n\\[ n = 9 - 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 3 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute $n = 3$ back into the set to find the values of the numbers:\n\\[ \\{3, 3 + 5, 3 + 6, 3 + 9, 3 + 15\\} = \\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the mean of the set:\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18}{5} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{50}{5} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = 10 \\]\n\nThus, the mean of the set is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
